the fire ox is the first instantiation  of a vehicle that's geared towards first  responders in this case particularly  firefighters you can remote control the  vehicle like a large toy car where you  take literally a game style controller  and drive the vehicle remotely where you  want to go but you don't actually have  to be on the vehicle  we have a large water tank on the system  we have a remote control nozzle we also  have a pump we have the ability to  dispense water while the vehicle is  moving this machine can be used to fight  wildland fire to get into situations  where you have tricky winds or areas  where a shifting fire is also very  useful for high-risk structure fire  situations you can use it in situations  where it's too risky to put the  firefighters in close proximity to the  fire or to other hazardous materials the  development of the fire arcs has not  been nearly that expensive we actually  repurposed a base vehicle that we sent  to Afghanistan and got back in one piece  because this is a variant of a prototype  that's not really in production yet  there's a real challenge for my team to  figure out how to build small numbers of  these vehicles at an affordable cost  that first responders could buy we see a  time when these systems will save lives  to help prevent injuries if we can  figure out how to do more with less how  you could let the machine do the work of  some of the firefighters then you can  help them where they are so challenged  on their budget from
 

